lines=['# Native prompt-control extension','', 'None of the three tested checkpoints reliably followed the requested primitive in these two noncontact states. The important finding is broader than a strict pose-tolerance failure: opposite axis instructions did not reverse endpoint direction, and paired open/close instructions did not reverse the gripper classification. This small diagnostic does not show that fine-tuning caused the problem.','', '## Protocol','', 'Ten conditions (native reference, hold, open, close, and world ±X/±Y/±Z), two archived noncontact states, three identical saved diffusion-noise tensors, and three checkpoints produced 180 offline action chunks. The six directional instructions request 30 mm while preserving wrist orientation and the already-open gripper. All non-language tensors were checked equal within each checkpoint/state; text was replaced rather than appended to a contradictory goal. No commands were executed.','', 'Vanilla uses its qualified native domain-3 RGB/object-crop route, 128-token text and concatenated rotation interface. V3/V4 use their domain-29 route with sparse history, crosshair/held annotation, physical-time projection and 256-token text. These channel differences prevent a clean across-model attribution to fine-tuning. The same 3 saved noise arrays were explicitly inserted at each generator\'s random-noise boundary.','', '## Partial and full effects','', '| Model | Correct sign, individually | Both signs in matched pair | Open gripper only | Close gripper only | Both open/close in pair | Full primitive |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
